{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqsexg8x2ff","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Agentic search context delivery clip fixed via fuller content field","summary":"Root cause of the our-way-prod arm answering \"I don't know\" on LongMemEval Oracle despite the grader keeping the right chunk: the context delivered to the answerer was clipped to the 200-char display summary BEFORE reaching context_deps. In lib/search/memory-search.js result.summary is set via slice(0,200); in lib/subconscious/index.js rankResults runs every result through compactResult which drops all unlisted fields and reclips to 240; contextDependencyFromResult then emits summary.slice(0,240), a no-op. Source chunks (lib/note-source-cluster.js CHUNK_CHARS=1200) hold the full answer-bearing text in node.summary, so 200 chars dropped most of the chunk and truncated the answer. Fix (token-aware, agentic-path only): searchUrlForPlan sets full_content=1 (only the subconscious agentic paths build that URL; one-shot GET /search never sets it). compileSearchContext on that flag attaches a bounded content field (<=1200) from the live node text, leaving the 200-char display summary untouched. compactResult preserves content (bounded). contextDependencyFromResult emits content as the delivered summary when present, else the prior 240 clip. Verified by direct HTTP repro against the worktree daemon at commit 00806352: POST /subconscious/search-context returned context_deps with summary_len=1200 and the GPS text present, while GET /search stayed at summary_len=200 with no content field. Two harness gotchas for verifying worktree lib changes on Windows: (1) zonoid_bench _find_daemon_js prefers a daemon.js whose sibling node_modules/@xenova exists, so a git worktree without node_modules falls back to the MAIN repo daemon.js and would not exercise the worktree fix; create a node_modules directory junction in the worktree to the main repo node_modules so the worktree daemon.js wins. (2) The bench embedded daemon exits co